1. Examining state and local governments that have successfully reduced the influence of money in politics, as there may be lessons applicable to federal lawmaking;
2. Investigate the effectiveness of transparency measures in other countries and assess how these innovations could be adapted to improve the functioning of US governing bodies;
3. Study rank-choice/preferential voting systems utilized abroad that prioritize voter intentions over arbitrary district boundaries created by gerrymandering;

1. Examining state and local governments that have successfully reduced the influence of money in politics, as there may be lessons applicable to federal lawmaking;
2. Investigate the effectiveness of transparency measures in other countries and assess how these innovations could be adapted to improve the functioning of US governing bodies;
3. Study rank-choice/preferential voting systems utilized abroad that prioritize voter intentions over arbitrary district boundaries created by gerrymandering;

4. Conduct research on successful public financing models employed overseas and analyze the ramifications of implementing similar systems domestically;
5. Explore alternative forms of election security protocols, such as independent voter verification systems, to combat voter fraud while ensuring easy accessibility for eligible voters;
6. Establish alliances with multidisciplinary scholars and practitioners to incorporate diverse expertise in policy suggestions, drawing insights from fields ranging from economics to sociology; last

